<?xml version="1.0"?>
<!--
  FALCON V2 - POWERED_FREE_FLIGHT_SMOKE_TEST, GUI reproduction world
  (gazebo-testing, 2026-08-23).

  Purpose: give tests/gazebo/scripts/run_powered_free_flight_gui.sh a world
  file that reproduces, in the interactive gz sim GUI, the initial condition
  of the already-PASSED POWERED_FREE_FLIGHT_SMOKE_TEST (headless
  gz.sim8.TestFixture run, driver script no longer in the repo per that
  task's own no-repo-changes requirement). This file does NOT modify
  model/model.sdf, any plugin, or any docs/source_of_truth/ value - it only
  places the unmodified model/model.sdf at a starting altitude/velocity and
  attaches ordinary, stock gz-sim GUI/control-surface-hold plugins that are
  standard test/launcher infrastructure, not aircraft physics.

  ===========================================================================
  HOW THE INITIAL CONDITION IS REPRODUCED (read before editing)
  ===========================================================================
  The original smoke test reached its initial condition via (1) a one-time
  world-pose teleport to altitude, then (2) a ~0.5s/500-step
  aero_lib.hold_step() proportional force/torque controller converging
  base_link onto the exact target body velocity, then (3) release to free
  6-DOF flight. That technique exists because TestFixture's Python API has
  no clean way to set a link's initial linear/angular velocity directly
  (Link.set_linear_velocity()/set_angular_velocity() were found, and
  documented in aero_lib.py's header comment, to freeze all further physics
  integration on that link once the calling script stops invoking them -
  unusable for "set once, then let it fly free").

  This world file uses a DIFFERENT, but physically equivalent and more
  precise, mechanism available at the plain-SDF level: SDF's
  <world><state><model><link><velocity> element, which gz-sim applies ONCE
  at entity-creation time as a genuine initial condition (not a per-tick
  Cmd override) - empirically confirmed this pass (gazebo-testing) to NOT
  exhibit the TestFixture Cmd-setter's "frozen link" behavior: a probe world
  using only this element showed base_link's world position evolving
  smoothly under real integration from the very first step (position and
  altitude both changing tick-to-tick exactly as expected from the
  commanded body velocity, with gravity/aero free to act throughout). Since
  the model spawns at zero attitude (identity orientation, matching the
  original smoke test's own level teleport), body-frame velocity ==
  world-frame velocity at t=0, so the u/w numbers below can be written
  directly into this world-frame element. This gives an EXACT, ZERO-ERROR,
  ZERO-TRANSIENT reproduction of the original scenario's steady-state
  initial condition - strictly more precise than the original 0.5s
  convergence-controller phase (which by construction has residual
  convergence error), at the cost of not modeling that phase's artificial
  hold-force transient, which was a TestFixture-technique artifact, not
  itself part of the aircraft physics under test. This deviation is
  intentional and is called out again in run_powered_free_flight_gui.sh.

  Initial condition values (bit-for-bit identical to the already-verified
  numbers used by tests/gazebo/scripts/test_trim_benchmarks.py's Benchmark B
  and by the original smoke test - not re-derived here):
    u = 18.14534 m/s, v = 0, w = -0.78335 m/s  (V=18.162 m/s, alpha=2.472deg)
    altitude = 85 m, level attitude (0 0 0 rad)
    left_elevator_joint = right_elevator_joint = +0.13962634 rad (+8.0 deg
      physical joint angle -> delta_e_aero=-8deg via the verified
      elevator_sign=-1.0 mapping, aero_v1_config.yaml)
    ailerons = 0, rudder = 0
    left/right throttle = 0.50/0.50 (commanded continuously by
      powered_free_flight_gui_setup.py once the server is up - SDF has no
      element for an initial gz-transport topic value)

  ===========================================================================
  CONTROL-SURFACE JOINT HOLD (JointPositionController, one per surface)
  ===========================================================================
  The 5 control-surface joints (left/right_aileron_joint,
  left/right_elevator_joint, rudder_joint) are, per model/model.sdf's own
  documented STRUCTURAL V1 design, ~1g massless-numerical free hinges with
  NO actuator and NO damping (TEMPORARY_NUMERICAL_MASS, see model.sdf). The
  original smoke test held them at their commanded angle every step via
  direct ECM position/velocity resets (aero_lib.pin_child_joints() /
  propulsion_lib.pin_control_surface_joints()) - a TestFixture-only
  mechanism with no live-server equivalent. This world file attaches the
  stock gz-sim JointPositionController system (one instance per surface,
  via <include><plugin>, exactly as SDF's own include.sdf schema supports)
  as the live-server equivalent: a plain PID position hold driven by
  Double commands published on each surface's own topic below. Gains are
  deliberately small (matching each surface's real ~1e-7..1e-5 kg*m^2
  hinge-axis inertia, queried from the live entity state this pass) so the
  hold is gentle rather than artificially stiff. This is a TEST-HARNESS
  SERVO-HOLD REPRESENTATION ONLY (exactly the same role pin_child_joints()
  already plays elsewhere in this suite) - it is not a claim about the real
  control-surface actuator, and it applies no force to base_link or to
  flight dynamics; it only keeps each surface link at its commanded angle
  so AerodynamicsSystem (which reads joint position, never joint velocity
  or torque) sees the correct control input. No aerodynamic, propulsion,
  mass, CG, inertia, or control-sign-mapping parameter is touched.

  left_aileron_joint  cmd_pos topic: /model/falcon_v2/control_surface/left_aileron/cmd_pos
  right_aileron_joint cmd_pos topic: /model/falcon_v2/control_surface/right_aileron/cmd_pos
  left_elevator_joint cmd_pos topic: /model/falcon_v2/control_surface/left_elevator/cmd_pos
  right_elevator_joint cmd_pos topic: /model/falcon_v2/control_surface/right_elevator/cmd_pos
  rudder_joint        cmd_pos topic: /model/falcon_v2/control_surface/rudder/cmd_pos

  Once free flight begins, NOTHING holds base_link itself - no velocity
  hold, no P-controller, no kinematic stabilization, no attitude
  controller, no external holding force is ever applied to base_link by
  this world file or by powered_free_flight_gui_setup.py. Gravity,
  FalconV2Aerodynamics, and FalconV2Propulsion (both already attached to
  model/model.sdf, unmodified here) are the only forces acting on the
  airframe - genuinely free 6-DOF flight.

  Physics/gravity match the existing falcon_v2_freefall_world.sdf
  (max_step_size 0.001s, gravity 0 0 -9.81), except real_time_factor is 1
  here (not 0/unlimited) so the GUI is watchable in real time.
-->
<sdf version="1.9">
  <world name="falcon_v2_powered_free_flight_gui">
    <physics name="1ms" type="dartsim">
      <max_step_size>0.001</max_step_size>
      <real_time_factor>1</real_time_factor>
    </physics>
    <gravity>0 0 -9.81</gravity>

    <plugin filename="gz-sim-physics-system" name="gz::sim::systems::Physics"></plugin>
    <plugin filename="gz-sim-scene-broadcaster-system" name="gz::sim::systems::SceneBroadcaster"></plugin>
    <plugin filename="gz-sim-user-commands-system" name="gz::sim::systems::UserCommands"></plugin>

    <!--
      Standard gz-sim GUI layout (3D scene + scene manager + interactive/
      camera-tracking view control + world control/stats + entity
      selection) - the same stock plugin set used by gz-sim's own example
      worlds. camera_pose gives a reasonable initial chase-ish view of the
      spawn point (0 0 85); see run_powered_free_flight_gui.sh's startup
      message for how to select falcon_v2 and follow it if this framing
      isn't ideal once the aircraft starts moving.
    -->
    <gui fullscreen="0">
      <plugin filename="MinimalScene" name="3D View">
        <gz-gui>
          <title>3D View</title>
          <property type="bool" key="showTitleBar">false</property>
          <property type="string" key="state">docked</property>
        </gz-gui>
        <engine>ogre2</engine>
        <scene>scene</scene>
        <ambient_light>0.4 0.4 0.4</ambient_light>
        <background_color>0.7 0.8 0.9</background_color>
        <camera_pose>-25 -15 92 0 0.12 0.5</camera_pose>
      </plugin>
      <plugin filename="GzSceneManager" name="Scene Manager">
        <gz-gui>
          <property key="resizable" type="bool">false</property>
          <property key="width" type="double">5</property>
          <property key="height" type="double">5</property>
          <property key="state" type="string">floating</property>
          <property key="showTitleBar" type="bool">false</property>
        </gz-gui>
      </plugin>
      <plugin filename="InteractiveViewControl" name="Interactive view control">
        <gz-gui>
          <property key="resizable" type="bool">false</property>
          <property key="width" type="double">5</property>
          <property key="height" type="double">5</property>
          <property key="state" type="string">floating</property>
          <property key="showTitleBar" type="bool">false</property>
        </gz-gui>
      </plugin>
      <plugin filename="CameraTracking" name="Camera Tracking">
        <gz-gui>
          <property key="resizable" type="bool">false</property>
          <property key="width" type="double">5</property>
          <property key="height" type="double">5</property>
          <property key="state" type="string">floating</property>
          <property key="showTitleBar" type="bool">false</property>
        </gz-gui>
      </plugin>
      <plugin filename="WorldControl" name="World control">
        <gz-gui>
          <title>World control</title>
          <property type="bool" key="showTitleBar">false</property>
          <property type="bool" key="resizable">false</property>
          <property type="double" key="height">72</property>
          <property type="double" key="width">121</property>
          <property type="string" key="state">floating</property>
          <anchors target="3D View">
            <line own="left" target="left"/>
            <line own="bottom" target="bottom"/>
          </anchors>
        </gz-gui>
        <play_pause>true</play_pause>
        <step>true</step>
        <start_paused>false</start_paused>
      </plugin>
      <plugin filename="WorldStats" name="World stats">
        <gz-gui>
          <title>World stats</title>
          <property type="bool" key="showTitleBar">false</property>
          <property type="bool" key="resizable">false</property>
          <property type="double" key="height">110</property>
          <property type="double" key="width">290</property>
          <property type="string" key="state">floating</property>
          <anchors target="3D View">
            <line own="right" target="right"/>
            <line own="bottom" target="bottom"/>
          </anchors>
        </gz-gui>
        <sim_time>true</sim_time>
        <real_time>true</real_time>
        <real_time_factor>true</real_time_factor>
        <iterations>true</iterations>
      </plugin>
      <plugin filename="EntityContextMenuPlugin" name="Entity context menu">
        <gz-gui>
          <property key="state" type="string">floating</property>
          <property key="width" type="double">5</property>
          <property key="height" type="double">5</property>
          <property key="showTitleBar" type="bool">false</property>
        </gz-gui>
      </plugin>
      <plugin filename="SelectEntities" name="Select Entities">
        <gz-gui>
          <property key="resizable" type="bool">false</property>
          <property key="width" type="double">5</property>
          <property key="height" type="double">5</property>
          <property key="state" type="string">floating</property>
          <property key="showTitleBar" type="bool">false</property>
        </gz-gui>
      </plugin>
    </gui>

    <light type="directional" name="sun">
      <cast_shadows>true</cast_shadows>
      <pose>0 0 150 0 0 0</pose>
      <diffuse>0.8 0.8 0.8 1</diffuse>
      <specular>0.2 0.2 0.2 1</specular>
      <direction>-0.5 0.1 -0.9</direction>
    </light>

    <model name="ground_plane">
      <static>true</static>
      <link name="link">
        <collision name="collision">
          <geometry>
            <plane>
              <normal>0 0 1</normal>
              <size>2000 2000</size>
            </plane>
          </geometry>
        </collision>
        <visual name="visual">
          <geometry>
            <plane>
              <normal>0 0 1</normal>
              <size>2000 2000</size>
            </plane>
          </geometry>
          <material>
            <ambient>0.3 0.5 0.3 1</ambient>
            <diffuse>0.3 0.5 0.3 1</diffuse>
          </material>
        </visual>
      </link>
    </model>

    <include>
      <uri>file:///home/emirhan/Desktop/FalconV2/model</uri>
      <name>falcon_v2</name>
      <pose>0 0 85 0 0 0</pose>

      <!-- Servo-hold representation only - see header comment. Gains sized
           for each surface's real ~1e-7..1e-5 kg*m^2 hinge-axis inertia. -->
      <plugin filename="gz-sim-joint-position-controller-system" name="gz::sim::systems::JointPositionController">
        <joint_name>left_aileron_joint</joint_name>
        <topic>/model/falcon_v2/control_surface/left_aileron/cmd_pos</topic>
        <p_gain>0.01</p_gain>
        <i_gain>0.0</i_gain>
        <d_gain>0.0005</d_gain>
        <cmd_min>-0.2</cmd_min>
        <cmd_max>0.2</cmd_max>
      </plugin>
      <plugin filename="gz-sim-joint-position-controller-system" name="gz::sim::systems::JointPositionController">
        <joint_name>right_aileron_joint</joint_name>
        <topic>/model/falcon_v2/control_surface/right_aileron/cmd_pos</topic>
        <p_gain>0.01</p_gain>
        <i_gain>0.0</i_gain>
        <d_gain>0.0005</d_gain>
        <cmd_min>-0.2</cmd_min>
        <cmd_max>0.2</cmd_max>
      </plugin>
      <plugin filename="gz-sim-joint-position-controller-system" name="gz::sim::systems::JointPositionController">
        <joint_name>left_elevator_joint</joint_name>
        <topic>/model/falcon_v2/control_surface/left_elevator/cmd_pos</topic>
        <p_gain>0.01</p_gain>
        <i_gain>0.0</i_gain>
        <d_gain>0.0005</d_gain>
        <cmd_min>-0.2</cmd_min>
        <cmd_max>0.2</cmd_max>
      </plugin>
      <plugin filename="gz-sim-joint-position-controller-system" name="gz::sim::systems::JointPositionController">
        <joint_name>right_elevator_joint</joint_name>
        <topic>/model/falcon_v2/control_surface/right_elevator/cmd_pos</topic>
        <p_gain>0.01</p_gain>
        <i_gain>0.0</i_gain>
        <d_gain>0.0005</d_gain>
        <cmd_min>-0.2</cmd_min>
        <cmd_max>0.2</cmd_max>
      </plugin>
      <plugin filename="gz-sim-joint-position-controller-system" name="gz::sim::systems::JointPositionController">
        <joint_name>rudder_joint</joint_name>
        <topic>/model/falcon_v2/control_surface/rudder/cmd_pos</topic>
        <p_gain>0.01</p_gain>
        <i_gain>0.0</i_gain>
        <d_gain>0.0005</d_gain>
        <cmd_min>-0.2</cmd_min>
        <cmd_max>0.2</cmd_max>
      </plugin>
      <!-- left_prop_joint / right_prop_joint are intentionally NOT given a
           JointPositionController - FalconV2Propulsion already owns their
           angular velocity every tick (plugins/propulsion/README.md). -->
    </include>

    <!-- One-time initial body velocity for base_link - see header comment. -->
    <state world_name="falcon_v2_powered_free_flight_gui">
      <model name="falcon_v2">
        <link name="base_link">
          <velocity>18.14534 0 -0.78335 0 0 0</velocity>
        </link>
      </model>
    </state>
  </world>
</sdf>
